  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Motors obligated $621M in FY2026 to date from federal contracts. General Motors received a total of 13,654 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $45.5K and year-over-year change up 120.6%. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and the page notes that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Fiscal-year obligations show a pattern across six years: FY21 $187M, FY22 $188M, FY23 $260M, FY24 $182M, FY25 $282M, and FY26 $621M. General Motors saw the FY26 total at $621M compared with prior years listed individually. Readers should treat the FY26 figure as a partial, fiscal year to date total. The numbers above are direct contract obligations recorded for the vendor and reflect the vendor-level activity captured for the selected period.",
